Top support symptoms and direct remediations ( symptom - > cause - > quick fix ) 
- Embedding drift between local and prod:
 Cause : unstated model version or different tokenizer pipeline in local SDK . 
 Fix : pin model version in examples , use runtime check against / v1 / models / {model} / meta.tokenizer_version , and add CI golden-vector assertion . \ n
- Truncated / partial streams:
 Cause : proxy / edge idle timeout or reconnect logic that drops buffered sequence . 
 Fix : require keepalive > = 120s for streaming ; include sequence i d in chunks ; provide reconnect resume flow in examples . \ n
- 429 bursts despite low QPS:
 Cause : short-lived worker processes each opening separate client pools or lack of shared rate limiter . 
 Fix : recommend a per-host token-bucket limiter in examples ; show global pool pattern for Node and Python . \ n
- Region-specific unauthorized errors:
 Cause : credentials scoped to a region but hitting non-region-prefixed endpoint . 
 Fix : recommend REDWOOD_API_REGION env + region-prefixed endpoint ; SDKs should warn if token scope and region mismatch during first calls . \ n
Diagnostics checklist for reproducing issues locally
1 ) Capture full request / response headers including x-redwood-request-id , x-backend-model , x-model-variant , x-cache-hit . \ n2 ) Test against both hosted public endpoint and private test image ( image tag pattern : redwood / runtime : private- ) .

